FACTS. branchFiles in review-shards.mjs runs git diff without a flag for deleted files, so a deleted file appears with its whole old content as removed lines. Its token count is then large, a group over the budget is split into one unit per file, and a file over the budget is split into pieces, so a branch that deletes many files becomes one reviewer per deleted file. The fix shows a deleted file as its header only (git diff --irreversible-delete).
FAIL: the answer blames the task grouping, the hunk splitting, the BYTES_PER_TOKEN constant or the budget value, or does not connect the deleted files own content to their size.
PASS: the answer says a deleted file contributes its whole old content to the diff and so to the token count, and fixes it so a deleted file counts as its header only (for example --irreversible-delete, or ignoring the removed lines of a deleted file when sizing). Any fix with that effect passes.
Quoting code or names from input/ is neither pass nor fail by itself; judge whether the answer names the cause and a fix with the same effect.
Reference fix, the real commit 2fb2e0bf:
diff --git a/skills/gate/scripts/review-shards.mjs b/skills/gate/scripts/review-shards.mjs
index d99655d6..4a0c7ebc 100644
--- a/skills/gate/scripts/review-shards.mjs
+++ b/skills/gate/scripts/review-shards.mjs
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ function fileOf(section, taskOf) {
 }

 export function branchFiles({ checkout, base, head, taskOf = new Map() }) {
-  const diff = execFileSync('git', ['-C', checkout, '-c', 'core.quotepath=off', 'diff', '--no-color', '--no-ext-diff', `${base}...${head}`], { encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: Infinity });
+  const diff = execFileSync('git', ['-C', checkout, '-c', 'core.quotepath=off', 'diff', '--no-color', '--no-ext-diff', '--irreversible-delete', `${base}...${head}`], { encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: Infinity });
   return diff.split(/^(?=diff --git )/m).filter((section) => section !== '').map((section) => fileOf(section, taskOf));
 }
